  "note": "Milano Centrale faces Piazza Duca d’Aosta with a pale limestone portico, three open entrance bays and a taller barrel-roofed concourse. Five glazed train sheds shelter 24 mapped track positions and a raised deck of boarding platforms. The model uses a 132 m sea-level datum. A cutout limited to the station portico and platform deck clears standard terrain from the model surfaces. The north apron tapers toward the host rail approach. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
